# Credentials known to have appeared in this repository, by SHA-256 of the
# literal value. The VALUES are never written here — that would defeat the file.
#
# FORMAT:  <sha256>  <max-occurrences>  <name>  # note
#
# `max-occurrences` is a RATCHET, not a target. A count that grows fails the
# check; a count that shrinks is a fix, and the number is lowered in the same
# commit that shrinks it. Zero means the literal must never appear.
#
# Compute a candidate's hash without writing it down:
#   printf '%s' "$SECRET" | sha256sum

44acccf4a551b57fac8a0aed1fb56bbfac849abefeae735afb199f1704dec48e  0  ODDS_API_KEY (exhausted free tier)
# Redacted 2026-08-25 from docs/CC-CMD-2026-06-29-odds-adapter-proof-p1.md:159,
# docs/source-registry.json:94 and outbox/cc-odds-audit-results.md (2 lines).
#
# All four were PROSE, not configuration: the source-registry hit was inside a
# `notes` string, and smoke.js reads that file only for
# `.includes('bsd-bzzoiro-soccer')`, so nothing loaded the key from it.
#
# Zero, because the key is dead and the relay stopped compiling it in on
# 2026-08-25 (field-relay-nba 0607526). This file exists because that change was
# reported as "the Odds API key is out of the repo" while three occurrences sat
# here, unscanned — the relay's checker only ever walked the relay.

c3118a4a99dfe805e724cc1da7bba35635e0c09341bf1a25ca9a6fb01e614638  9  RELAY_SHARED_SECRET (relay cron/self-call shared secret)
# NOT zero, and deliberately so. Nine occurrences, of which THREE are live code:
#
#   workers/field-claude-proxy/src/index.js:105
#       `env.RELAY_SHARED_SECRET || '<literal>'` — an auth comparison. The env
#       read already exists; the literal is its fallback.
#   scripts/seed-mls-return-2026.py:17
#   scripts/seed-mls-tournaments-2026.py:21
#       bare literals in an X-FIELD-Relay header aimed at POST /d1/execute
#   retry_telemetry_probe.js:37
#       same, a fourth live site
#
# The remaining five are prose: CONTRACTS.md:245, three CC-CMDs, one root-cause
# doc.
#
# Removing them WITHOUT rotating first buys nothing — the value is in git
# history either way. The order is written down in field-relay-nba
# docs/CC-CMD-2026-08-25-rotate-relay-secret.md, and it is SOURCE-FIRST: while
# the value is unchanged, replacing a literal with a binding holding the same
# value is a runtime no-op that can be verified live, whereas rotate-first makes
# every site wrong at once.
#
# That CC-CMD counted 114 sites in the relay alone. These nine are additional
# and are named there now.
